 with the complete information. Availability is restricted and the event might be called off if participation is insufficient.","startDate":"2026-10-02T15:45:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-2-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"HGXP+XM Toronto","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Toronto","addressRegion":"ON","addressCountry":"ca","streetAddress":"HGXP+XM Toronto, Toronto, ON"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Casual Moves and Coffee House Chess","url":"https://www.meetup.com/casual-moves-and-coffee-house-chess/"},"performer":"Casual Moves and Coffee House Chess"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"GHOST TOUR - 👻 The Ghosts of University of Toronto 🎃 with Dinner!","url":"https://www.meetup.com/torontotnt/events/316624518/","description":"# 🎃 The Ghosts of the University of Toronto 👻\n\n### A 90-Minute Halloween Ghost Walk Through Toronto's Haunted History\n\nL\nooking for something a little different this Halloween season?\n\nJoin us for a **guided ghost walk through the University of Toronto campus and its eerie surroundings**, exploring some of the stories, legends, and strange histories hidden in one of Toronto's oldest neighbourhoods.\nThis isn't one of our regular walks where we're simply following a trail and enjoying the scenery.\n\n**This is a curated storytelling experience.**\n\nI've researched the locations, developed the route, and put together the stories specifically for this experience. We'll explore some of the darker corners of the university and surrounding neighbourhoods while uncovering the people, places, and legends that have given them their haunted reputations.\n\n🕯️ Along the way, we'll hear stories about:\n\n* What the Christies — yes, *Mr. Christie Cookies* — were hiding in their mansion 🍪\n* The restless little girl who is never happy 👧\n* What might really be lurking inside Queen's Park 👀\n* Haunted stories connected to University of Toronto buildings\n* The Royal Conservatory of Music\n* The Royal Ontario Museum\n* And some other stories that are better experienced after dark... 👻\n\nYou don't have to believe in ghosts.\nYou just have to enjoy a good story.\n\n📱 Don't forget to join our **WhatsApp Group – [CLICK HERE](https://chat.whatsapp.com/H59mSCbsAi018gYANrKAnc)**\n\n***\n\n## 👻 What We'll Do\n\nWe'll spend approximately **90 minutes walking through the University of Toronto campus and surrounding streets**, stopping at locations connected to Toronto's haunted history.\n\nAlong the way we'll:\n\n* Hear stories about some of Toronto's most intriguing characters and locations\n* Explore the darker history of the University of Toronto\n* Visit locations associated with ghost stories and local legends\n* Learn the history behind some of the buildings around us\n* Walk through Queen's Park and the surrounding area\n* Finish at the **Royal Ontario Museum**\n\nWe'll remain **outside the buildings** throughout the experience.\nThe walking pace will be moderate, with plenty of stops along the way for stories.\n\n***\n\n## 🕯️ This Is More Than a Walk\n\nOur regular walks are about getting outside, exploring Toronto, and meeting people.\nThis one is different.\n\n**This is a guided storytelling experience.**\n\nThe route and stories have been researched and developed specifically for this event, so you're not just following me from one location to another — you're getting a story about the city as we go.\nAnd because it's Halloween season, we'll be doing it after dark. 🎃\n\n***\n\n## 🍂 What to Expect\n\nThis is an outdoor walking experience, so please dress appropriately for the weather.\nWe'll be walking for approximately **90 minutes**, with regular stops for storytelling.\n\nThere is **no entry into any buildings**, so you won't need to worry about museum admission or other entrance fees.\nAnd while some of the stories are genuinely creepy, this isn't designed to be a horror attraction.\n\nIt's **Toronto history, local legends, and storytelling with a spooky twist.**\n\n***\n\n## 🧢 Meetup Details\n\n📍 **Meeting Location:** In front of the building by the stairs\n🫎 **Look for me in my Moose Hat!**\n⏰ **Start Time:** 7:00 PM sharp\nI will only wait **5 minutes.**\n**Early is on time. On time is late.**\n🚶‍♂️ **Walking Pace:** Moderate\n🏁 **End Point:** Royal Ontario Museum\n\n***\n\n## 🎟️ Meetup Fee\n\n**$10 cash or e-transfer**\n📧 **mathewmaclean@hotmail.com**\n\nThis is a **curated, guided storytelling experience**, rather than one of our regular group walks. The route, stories, and history have been researched and developed specifically for this experience.\n\nFood and drinks afterward are optional and are **not included** in the Meetup fee.\n\n***\n\n## 🍻 After the Ghost Walk\n\nWe'll finish at the **Royal Ontario Museum**.\n\nFor anyone who wants to keep the evening going, we'll walk about 10 minutes over to the **Duke of York** for food, drinks, and conversation.\n\nYou don't have to come — but everyone is welcome.\nBecause sometimes the best part of a ghost story is having someone to talk about it with afterward. 👻\n\n***\n\n## 🌈 Who Is This For?\n\nThis is great for:\n\n* Anyone who loves ghost stories 👻\n* History buffs\n* People curious about Toronto's darker side\n* Fans of Halloween\n* Anyone who enjoys storytelling\n* People looking for something different to do in the city\n* Anyone who wants to meet new people while exploring Toronto\n\nYou don't need to believe in ghosts.\n**Just bring your curiosity.**\n\nYou're welcome to RSVP ahead of time or just show up on the day if you're unsure about your schedule.\nSometimes things happen and events may need to be cancelled or changed, so please keep an eye on the event page for updates.\n👤 **Organizer: Mathew**\n\nQuestions? Post on the event wall or email:\n📧 **torontomoviesandoutings@hotmail.com**\n\n**Come for the ghosts. 👻**\n**Stay for the stories.**\n**Leave with a new connection — and maybe a new friend.** 🖤","startDate":"2026-10-02T23:00:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-2-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"Queen's Park Legislative Assembly of Ontario","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Toronto","addressRegion":"ON","addressCountry":"ca","streetAddress":"1 Queens Park, Toronto, ON M7A 1A2, Canada, Toronto, ON"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Try New Things in Toronto!","url":"https://www.meetup.com/torontotnt/"},"performer":"Try New Things in Toronto!"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"GHOST TOUR - 👻 The Ghosts of University of Toronto 🎃  with Dinner! ","url":"https://www.meetup.com/no-such-thing-as-bad-weather/events/316200432/","description":"# 🎃 The Ghosts of the University of Toronto 👻\n\n### A 90-Minute Halloween Ghost Walk Through Toronto's Haunted History\n\nL\nooking for something a little different this Halloween season?\n\nJoin us for a **guided ghost walk through the University of Toronto campus and its eerie surroundings**, exploring some of the stories, legends, and strange histories hidden in one of Toronto's oldest neighbourhoods.\nThis isn't one of our regular walks where we're simply following a trail and enjoying the scenery.\n\n**This is a curated storytelling experience.**\n\nI've researched the locations, developed the route, and put together the stories specifically for this experience. We'll explore some of the darker corners of the university and surrounding neighbourhoods while uncovering the people, places, and legends that have given them their haunted reputations.\n\n🕯️ Along the way, we'll hear stories about:\n\n* What the Christies — yes, *Mr. Christie Cookies* — were hiding in their ma